cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DINOH — a Digital, AI-assisted Infrastructure for Oral History: public evaluation release (multilingual evaluation harness)"
abstract: >-
  A multilingual, human-referenced evaluation harness for the C²DH Oral History
  Workflow. It provides the hand-annotated synthetic gold standard, the JSON schemas,
  the per-field-type metric design and the tested scoring path for evaluating AI
  proposals on two narrow, assistive tasks — minimal metadata extraction and thematic
  segmentation (WindowDiff, Pk) — reported per language across German, English, French,
  Italian, Spanish, Luxembourgish, and Portuguese, on synthetic data. Includes WebVTT
  and OHMS interoperability exporters and a concept & architecture note. Note: the model
  backend is stubbed in this release, so the artefacts under reports/ are smoke-test
  output of the scoring path and not model-performance results; this release makes
  measurement possible rather than reporting measurements.
